    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 run, 0 failures). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded customer-code de-duplication so that when a computed `customerCode` collides with an existing owner's, it gets `-<n>` (smallest `n \u2265 2` that's free) appended.\n\nEach piece went where it belongs:\n\n- **`OwnerRepository.findByCustomerCode(String)`** \u2014 a new finder mirroring the existing `findByTelephone`/`findByEmail`, implemented in all three backends (`SpringDataOwnerRepository`, `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl`, `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`) to keep the interface consistent. Only the active `spring-data-jpa` profile runs in tests, but the others stay in sync.\n\n- **`CustomerCode.deduplicate(base, Predicate<String> taken)`** \u2014 the pure string logic (return `base`, else smallest free `base-<n>`) lives in the model alongside `of`/`regionOf`, with the DB lookup passed in as a predicate so the model stays persistence-free. `regionOf` still reads the region correctly since it splits on the *first* `-`.\n\n- **`DeduplicateCustomerCode`** \u2014 a small single-responsibility OfficeFloor step that queries the repository and stores the unique code back on the owner. It's a separate step (not folded into `AssignCustomerCode`), mirroring the existing `AssignHouseholdId` \u2192 `EnsureUniqueHousehold` split.\n\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step between `assignCustomerCode` and `assignMembershipNumber` (under the same `transaction` governance), so the membership number and all other values derived from the whole code see the de-duplicated variant.\n\nThe `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` acceptance test passes.",
